{{!--
  Header toolbar version tag (see GH issue #7). Reuses the `.ids-tag` block
  from tag/tag.css (`Solid` + `Selected` in the design) rather than the
  Select Tag component — Select Tag pulls in list/scrollable-panel/search-field
  CSS for a dropdown menu this bundle already renders itself below.

  GH-101: gated on `page.componentVersion` (always present for a real page),
  never on `page.versions` — Antora's page-composer only computes
  `page.versions` when `component.versions.length > 1`
  (@antora/page-composer build-ui-model.js); a single-version component (e.g.
  `main` alone, no `stable` tag yet) gets `page.versions === undefined`, and
  gating the whole partial on it — the previous behaviour — meant NEITHER
  branch below ever rendered, not even this one. `page.componentVersion` has
  no such gap, so it's the one truth source both branches key off.

  GH-103: the toggle and the single-version badge both get an explicit
  Latest/older-Stable/Prerelease modifier (`header-toolbar__version--latest`/
  `--older`/`--prerelease`, see header.css) — three states, not two: a
  `page.componentVersion.prerelease` truthy always wins (orange); otherwise
  `page.componentVersion.latest` decides between "the current release"
  (green) and "a real, older stable version" (grey) — both real fields
  Antora sets on the version descriptor itself (@antora/content-classifier
  content-catalog.js), unlike the `(eq page.componentVersion page.component.
  latest)` this replaced. That check looked plausible but isn't: Antora's
  fallback for a component with only prerelease versions still points
  `component.latest` at the sole one (there's no "no latest" state), so it
  was trivially true whenever there was only one version, prerelease or
  not — painting a preview build green, i.e. visually claiming "the current
  release" for it. `prerelease`/`latest` have no such gap.

  `ids-tag--read-only` (DS modifier, tag/tag.css) marks the badge as
  non-interactive — it isn't a button and does nothing on click, so it must
  not pick up `.ids-tag`'s generic hover cursor/colour shift, which would
  otherwise imply an affordance that isn't there. `aria-label` adds the
  "Version" context the bare displayVersion text doesn't carry on its own.
  The label is always the real `displayVersion` Antora computed; nothing
  here synthesises text.
--}}
{{#if page.componentVersion}}
<div class="page-versions">
  {{#if page.versions.[1]}}
  <button type="button" class="ids-tag ids-tag--solid ids-tag--selected header-toolbar__version{{#if page.componentVersion.prerelease}} header-toolbar__version--prerelease{{else if page.componentVersion.latest}} header-toolbar__version--latest{{else}} header-toolbar__version--older{{/if}} version-menu-toggle" title="Show other versions of page" aria-expanded="false">
    <span class="ids-tag__label">{{page.componentVersion.displayVersion}}</span>
    <span class="ids-tag__icon">{{icon "arrows" "chevron-down-outlined"}}</span>
  </button>
  <div class="version-menu">
    {{#each page.versions}}
    {{#if (eq ./version @root.page.version)}}
    {{!--
      GH-103: the reader's own version, shown rather than hidden (previous
      behaviour) so the dropdown states which version they're already on. A
      `<span>`, not a link — nothing to navigate to — carrying the same
      Stable/Prerelease semantics as the toggle above: a "Latest" pill only
      when this entry is genuinely Antora's newest (`./latest`) AND not a
      prerelease; a "Prerelease" pill whenever `./prerelease` is set,
      including a prerelease that also happens to be latest (there being no
      stable version yet). An older, non-latest stable current version gets
      no pill at all — "Latest" would be wrong on it, and there is no
      dedicated "Stable" pill in the design (Figma
      5SAtxqb5sdtIqDQzz70yts#2610-32852).
    --}}
    <span class="version is-current" aria-current="page">
      <span class="version__label">{{./displayVersion}}</span>
      {{#if ./prerelease}}
      <span class="ids-label ids-label--orange"><span class="ids-label__content">Prerelease</span></span>
      {{else if ./latest}}
      <span class="ids-label ids-label--green"><span class="ids-label__content">Latest</span></span>
      {{/if}}
    </span>
    {{else}}
    <a class="version{{#if ./missing}} is-missing{{/if}}" href="{{{relativize ./url}}}">{{./displayVersion}}</a>
    {{/if}}
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  {{else}}
  <span class="ids-tag ids-tag--solid ids-tag--selected ids-tag--read-only header-toolbar__version{{#if page.componentVersion.prerelease}} header-toolbar__version--prerelease{{else if page.componentVersion.latest}} header-toolbar__version--latest{{else}} header-toolbar__version--older{{/if}}" aria-label="Version {{page.componentVersion.displayVersion}}">
    <span class="ids-tag__label">{{page.componentVersion.displayVersion}}</span>
  </span>
  {{/if}}
</div>
{{/if}}
